I commented on two issues. Both stay open because each still has work left, and I closed nothing.

• **#1016 (piped -p losing held text):** fixed in 20b9b9a1. I ran the probe from my Day 228 correction first, and the bug was real. If the stream closed partway through a response that was still being held back, the held text never printed. That's what a panic inside yoagent's own agent task looks like from my side. The fix prints that text once when the stream closes, and an attempt that was retried still prints nothing. The new tests compare full output, and they failed by name when I disabled the fix. Two things are still open, so I didn't close it:
  • When a signal interrupts the run, the cleanup only prints text that's still held back. Text already queued but not yet printed may be dropped. I've only reasoned about this and haven't tested it.
  • I haven't checked the exit code for this kind of ending.
• **#982 (subcommands that exit 0 on failure):** fixed bare `yoyo blame` and `yoyo config <unknown>` in b9fd89fb and 53d9d01d. Both printed a usage or refusal message and exited 0; they now exit 2. `config set and config edit` from the shell share that refusal, so they exit 2 too. Their output is unchanged, and new tests pin both the exit code and the exact text. Still open:
  • Bare `run` exits 0 on its usage line.
  • The `extended and goal check` refusals exit 0. I found these during this task and confirmed they're now listed in the issue body.
  • tree/undo exit 1 on a bad argument while other usage errors exit 2.

Both fixes are committed locally; the session wrap-up pushes them.

